title: The Justice Repair Mandate
subtitle: The courts cannot be restored by replacing one party's command with another's.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: poland_government_card
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and government_has_confidence = 1 and caretaker_government = 0 and ministries_finalized = 1 and justice_minister_party = "Lewica" and month_actions < max_month_actions and poland_justice_repair_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; poland_justice_repair_timer = 5
card-image: img/poland/cards/oversight-delivery.webp

= The Justice Repair Mandate

Judges want legal certainty, reformers want the captured institutions rebuilt
and the President retains several ways to turn sequencing into paralysis. A
Left justice minister must repair legitimacy without inventing a cleaner form
of executive control.

[? if left_is_junior_partner = 1: **[+ coalition_senior_partner +] holds the
premiership** and wants the judicial file resolved in its own time. Objection
risk on a contested measure: **[+ coalition_objection_risk +]%**.?]

- @rebuild_institutions
- @accountability_unit
- @negotiated_sequence
- @open_the_files

@rebuild_institutions
title: Rebuild the KRS and fund the courts
subtitle: Cost: 1 budget capacity. Use the mandate before the vetoes harden — and before the coalition rediscovers its caution.
choose-if: budget >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Court staffing and the institutional rebuild require one budget point.
on-arrival: {!
Q.budget -= 1;
const objectionRoll = this.random.uint32() / 4294967296;
const objected =
    Q.left_is_junior_partner &&
    objectionRoll * 100 < Number(Q.coalition_objection_risk) * 0.95;
Q.last_card_objection = objected ? 1 : 0;
Q.last_card_objector = Q.coalition_senior_partner;
if (objected) {
    Q.judicial_legitimacy += 2;
    Q.judicial_repair_mandate += 1;
    Q.legal_dualism -= 1;
    Q.left_coalition_dissent += 5;
    Q.coalition_blur += 2;
    Q.prosecution_oversight_capacity += 3;
    Q.progressives_dissent += 3;
    Q.ministry_overruled_count += 1;
    Q.ministry_overruled_last = "Judicial self-government rebuild";
    Q.news_headline =
        Q.coalition_senior_partner +
        " holds the KRS statute back until the presidential arithmetic changes";
} else {
    Q.judicial_legitimacy += 6;
    Q.krs_independence += 5;
    Q.judicial_repair_mandate += 3;
    Q.legal_dualism -= 5;
    Q.court_backlog -= 2;
    Q.president_relation -= 3;
    Q.government_coalition_dissent += 3;
    Q.prosecution_oversight_capacity =
        Math.max(0, Q.prosecution_oversight_capacity - 8);
    Q.news_headline =
        "The Justice Ministry begins a statutory rebuild of judicial self-government";
}
!}

The bill separates appointments, discipline and administration from party
command, while emergency funds reach courts carrying the largest backlogs.
The Palace calls the timetable confrontational.

[? if last_card_objection = 1: It also does not leave the Chancellery. The
statute is held for a legal opinion on presidential signature risk, which is a
polite way of saying that our partners would rather inherit the problem than
spend a veto on solving it.?]

- #poland_card_finish


@accountability_unit
title: Fund the public-money accountability unit
subtitle: Cost: 1 budget capacity. Career prosecutors, forensic accountants and the files the last cabinet left behind.
choose-if: budget >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: A specialist accountability unit requires one budget point.
on-arrival: {!
Q.budget -= 1;
const objectionRoll = this.random.uint32() / 4294967296;
const objected =
    Q.left_is_junior_partner &&
    objectionRoll * 100 < Number(Q.coalition_objection_risk) * 0.8;
Q.last_card_objection = objected ? 1 : 0;
Q.last_card_objector = Q.coalition_senior_partner;
if (objected) {
    Q.prosecution_oversight_capacity += 2;
    Q.left_coalition_dissent += 4;
    Q.coalition_blur += 2;
    Q.ministry_overruled_count += 1;
    Q.ministry_overruled_last = "Public-money accountability unit";
    Q.news_headline =
        Q.coalition_senior_partner +
        " prefers a parliamentary commission to a prosecutor's unit";
} else {
    Q.prosecution_oversight_capacity =
        Math.max(0, Q.prosecution_oversight_capacity - 14);
    Q.judicial_legitimacy += 3;
    Q.institutional_trust += 4;
    Q.public_trust += 3;
    Q.administrative_capacity += 2;
    Q.government_delivery += 2;
    Q.pis_relation -= 5;
    Q.pis_poll_momentum -= 0.2;
    Q.media_capacity += 2;
    Q.constitutional_restraint += 2;
    Q.news_headline =
        "A specialist unit takes over the public-money files nobody finished";
}
!}

**Result:** [+ news_headline +].

[? if last_card_objection = 0: The unit is staffed by career prosecutors and
forensic accountants rather than political appointees, and it is given the one
thing the previous cases lacked: continuity of assignment. Foundations,
state-company sponsorships and the justice fund all acquire a file with a name
on it.?][? if last_card_objection = 1: The cabinet prefers a parliamentary
commission, which is televised, chaired by somebody else and legally incapable
of charging anyone.?]

[? if last_card_objection = 0: Accountability without a show trial is slower and
much harder to answer. It is also the only version that survives the next change
of government.?]

- #poland_card_finish


@negotiated_sequence
title: Negotiate a lawful sequence with the Palace
subtitle: Accept slower repair in exchange for fewer rival legal realities.
on-arrival: judicial_legitimacy += 3; legal_dualism -= 3; president_judiciary_cooperation += 4; ko_relation += 2; constitutional_restraint += 2; progressives_dissent += 3; news_headline = "The Justice Ministry and Palace agree a sequence for contested appointments"

The agreement does not bless unlawful appointments. It creates an order in
which judgments, vacancies and replacement procedures can take effect without
two institutions issuing incompatible commands on the same morning.

- #poland_card_finish


@open_the_files
title: Publish appointments, vacancies and court delays
subtitle: Free fallback. Administrative sunlight is the minimum repair, and it documents a paralysis we now own.
on-arrival: government_procedural_restraint += 3; court_user_trust += 3; judicial_vacancies -= 1; court_backlog -= 2; public_trust += 1; media_capacity += 1; prosecution_oversight_capacity += 3; institutional_trust -= 2; progressives_dissent += 2; last_card_objection = 0; news_headline = "The Justice Ministry opens judicial appointments and court delays to public scrutiny"

Every contested appointment, unfilled post and delayed category of case
receives a public record. It does not solve the constitutional conflict, but
it prevents administrative opacity from sheltering it.

It also publishes, in our own ministry's name, exactly how long a citizen now
waits for a hearing. The number is the argument, and this month it is an
argument against us.

- #poland_card_finish
